From: Analog Rytm MKII research
Subject: [PATCH] target/m68k: reset ColdFire EMAC MASK to all ones

The ColdFire EMAC MASK register resets to 0xffffffff. Leaving it zeroed
causes every EMAC-with-load effective address to be ANDed down to address
zero until guest software explicitly writes MASK.

diff --git a/target/m68k/cpu.c b/target/m68k/cpu.c
--- a/target/m68k/cpu.c
+++ b/target/m68k/cpu.c
@@ -110,6 +110,9 @@ static void m68k_cpu_reset_hold(Object *obj, ResetType type)
     }

     memset(env, 0, offsetof(CPUM68KState, end_reset_fields));
+    if (m68k_feature(env, M68K_FEATURE_CF_EMAC)) {
+        env->mac_mask = 0xffffffff;
+    }
 #ifdef CONFIG_USER_ONLY
     cpu_m68k_set_sr(env, 0);
 #else
